[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one bug: the parser reads dates month first. The reports merged into it
hold three problems. Each now has its own ticket, with how many reports it covers.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Fixing the parser closes only the first row.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} {repo} />

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant on file writes the
  day first. Engineering marked it fixed (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`).
- **`hint`**: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, so people type the month
  first, and the form reads it day first. The parser fix does not touch it. Engineering marked it
  won't fix because booking-v3 is retired, but the tenant directory still lists three tenants on
  `booking-v3`. Check before closing.
- **`one-day move`**: dates shifted by one day, or one meeting on different days in different time
  zones. That is not a month flip. The desk had already read these apart (`desk-notes.json`); the
  #4471 page counted them under `parser`. No fix yet.

## How the count works

- Reports are counted once per id: the export pages overlap.
- A report's cause comes from its tenant (locale and booking form, `causes.ts`), not from intake's
  tag, which is a guess from the reporter's browser.
- The one-day moves are taken out of their tenant's cause and counted on their own.

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone. Subjects like
"Wrong day on the invite" fit all three problems, so all three went into one ticket. Changing the
rule needs a new decision record; this page doesn't edit 0001.

